TI  - Bio-enzyme conversion method of L-phenylglycinol            comprises e.g. reacting reaction substrate 2-hydroxy            acetophenone solution, mixing fermentation liquor of            glucose dehydrogenase to perform conversion reaction,            adding reaction substrate 2-hydroxyacetophenone            solution, monitoring reaction endpoint
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - Bio-enzyme conversion method of                L-phenylglycinol comprises (i) selecting single                colony for lysogeny broth shake flask culture, and                performing enzyme cutting verification, introducing                to the biological worker for sequencing, correcting                the sequencing to obtain recombinant carrier 1,                (ii) mixing the fermentation liquor of glucose                dehydrogenase (BzGDH) to perform conversion                reaction (pH = 9.0), firstly adding amine donor                (isopropylamine or R-phenylethylamine), 5-pyridoxal                phosphate (PLP), (R) selective                omegaaminotransferase, glucose dehydrogenase in the                reaction process, adding 2-hydroxyacetophenone                solid, stopping adding 2-hydroxyacetophenone solid                (iii) adding the reaction substrate                2-hydroxyacetophenone solution (DMSO) for one time,                and (iv) controlling the pH value of the solution                in the reaction system at 8.6-9.2, and monitoring                the reaction endpoint through central control to                terminate the reaction and obtain transformation                solution.
                    USE - The method is useful for bio-enzyme conversion                method of L-phenylglycinol.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method greatly reduces the fermentation                cost and improves the enzyme activity, and                utilizing thalli in the biotransformation process                can be recycled for secondary use, which is good                for saving cost.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - Bio-enzyme conversion method of                L-phenylglycinol comprises (i) designing a pair of                primers Fp with nucleotides sequence of                5'-ggagagaattcatgggcatcgacactg-3'(EcoR I) (SEQ ID                NO: 3) and Rp with nucleotides sequence of                5'-gccggtcgactttaggccgcgtactga-3' (Sal I) (SEQ ID                NO: 4) by omega-aminotransferase (MVTA),                representing the base sequence of the enzyme                cutting site by underline, taking the Mycobacterium                vanbaaleniigenome as the template, utilizing PCR                method to amplify the target gene by using Fp and                Rp as primers, performing enzyme digestion on the                amplified target gene and plasmid pET-28a with                EcoRI and Sal I respectively, verifying the enzyme                digestion efficiency through gel electrophoresis,                recycling the target strip through the glue                recycling kit, mixing the recovered target gene                fragment with the vector fragment in a molar ratio                of 3:1, incubating at room temperature for 6-8                hours, and transforming into Escherichia coliBL21                (DH5&#945;), coating on lysogeny broth solid                culture medium containing kanamycin resistance,                culturing at 37&#176;C for 12 hours, selecting                single colony for lysogeny broth shake flask                culture, and performing enzyme cutting                verification, introducing to the biological worker                for sequencing, correcting the sequencing to obtain                recombinant carrier 1, (ii) utilizing the                recombinant vector 1 as a template, designing                primers Fa and Ra to amplify the T7 promoter and                GDH sequence, utilizing the method in (i) to make                Fa, connecting the target gene amplified by Ra with                the recombinant carrier 1, constructing recombinant                carrier 2, and transferring the successfully                constructed recombinant carrier 2 into Escherichia                coliBL21(DH5&#945;) to obtain recombinant                Escherichia coliBL21(DH5&#945;), where the                sequences of Fa with nucleotides sequence of                5'-ccgctcgagttatgtattcagatctagctgg-3' (XhoI) (SEQ                ID NO: 5) and Ra with nucleotides sequence of                5'-ccgctcgagcttttaaccgcgacccgcttgaaaac-3'(XhoI)                (SEQ ID NO: 6) respectively, transferring the                verified correct plasmid into Escherichia                coliBL21(DE3) to obtain a new bacterial strain,                culturing and collecting the cells and storing in                cold storage, (iii) reacting the reaction substrate                2-hydroxy acetophenone solution, amine donor                (isopropylamine or R-phenylethylamine), 5-pyridoxal                phosphate (PLP), (R) selective w-aminotransferase,                mixing the fermentation liquor of glucose                dehydrogenase (BzGDH) to perform conversion                reaction (pH = 9.0), firstly adding amine donor                (isopropylamine or R-phenylethylamine), 5-pyridoxal                phosphate (PLP), (R) selective                omegaaminotransferase, glucose dehydrogenase in the                reaction process, adding 2-hydroxyacetophenone                solid, stopping adding 2-hydroxyacetophenone solid                when the weight ratio of the 2-hydroxyacetophenone                solid and the reaction backing material reaches                1:0.5-0.8, (iv) adding the reaction substrate                2-hydroxyacetophenone solution (DMSO) for one time,                where the added amount is 2-7% of the volume of the                reaction system, (v) controlling the pH value of                the solution in the reaction system at 8.6-9.2, and                keeping the pH value not to be reduced to 7.5,                adjusting the pH of the solution by adding an amine                donor, and monitoring the reaction endpoint through                central control to terminate the reaction and                obtain transformation solution.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow chart of the method                for bio-enzyme conversion method of                L-phenylglycinol (Drawing includes non-English                language text).
