TI  - Preparing ascorbic acid glucoside useful in e.g.            preparing product with function of anti-aging involves            inoculating seed liquid to fermentation culture medium,            adding isopropyl beta-d-1-thiogalactopyranoside            inducing reaction, adding yeast to reaction solution,            filtering, and drying supernatant
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - Preparing ascorbic acid glucoside involves (1)                selecting pET-28a as plasmid vector, cloning the                coding gene of sucrose phosphorylase to pET-28a                vector, (2) taking E. coli BL21 (DE3) as host cell,                transferring the recombinant plasmid pET28a/SPase                into E. coli BL21 (DE3) competent cell, and coating                on lysogeny broth solid culture medium, (3)                inoculating the recombinant Escherichia coliE. coli                BL21 (DE3) /pET28a-SPase in lysogeny broth liquid                culture medium, inoculating the seed liquid to a                fermentation culture medium, adding isopropyl                &#946;- d-1-thiogalactopyranoside inducing                reaction for 15 hours, and centrifuging, (4) taking                the bacterial cell precipitate as biocatalyst,                taking sucrose and L-ascorbic acid as substrate to                form conversion system, and performing conversion                reaction, (5) adding yeast to the reaction solution                to culture, filtering and removing the solid matter                in the culture solution, and (6) crystallizing,                washing and drying the supernatant to obtain                ascorbic acid glucoside.
                    USE - The ascorbic acid glucoside is useful in                preparing product with at least one function of                whitening, removing spot, anti-aging, and repair                (claimed).
                    ADVANTAGE - The method greatly improves the yield of                ascorbic acid glucoside, and has simple,                high-efficiency, time-saving and                labor-saving.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - Preparing ascorbic acid glucoside involves (1)                selecting pET-28a as plasmid vector, cloning the                coding gene of sucrose phosphorylase to pET-28a                vector to obtain recombinant plasmid pET28a/SPase                containing sucrose phosphorylase gene, (2) taking                E. coli BL21 (DE3) as host cell, transferring the                recombinant plasmid pET28a/SPase into E. coli BL21                (DE3) competent cell, and coating on lysogeny broth                solid culture medium containing 50 &#181;g/ml                kanamycin to culture to obtain monoclonal colony,                transferring the monoclonal colony to lysogeny                broth liquid culture medium containing 50                &#181;g/ml kanamycin to cultivate to obtain                recombinant Escherichia coliE. coli BL21 (DE3)                /pET28a-SPase, (3) inoculating the recombinant                Escherichia coliE. coli BL21 (DE3) /pET28a-SPase in                lysogeny broth liquid culture medium containing 50                &#181;g/ml kanamycin to cultivate to obtain                seed liquid, inoculating the seed liquid to a                fermentation culture medium containing 50                &#181;g/ml of kanamycin to culture, adding                isopropyl &#946;- d-1-thiogalactopyranoside                inducing reaction for 15 hours when the bacteria                liquid biomass in the ferment culture medium to                OD600is 10-15, centrifuging, and collecting                bacterial cell precipitate, (4) taking the                bacterial cell precipitate as biocatalyst, taking                sucrose and L-ascorbic acid as substrate to form                conversion system, and performing conversion                reaction to obtain reaction liquid, (5) adding                yeast to the reaction solution to culture to obtain                culture solution, filtering and removing the solid                matter in the culture solution to obtain                supernatant, and (6) concentrating, crystallizing,                washing and drying the supernatant to obtain                ascorbic acid glucoside.INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are also included                for:an ascorbic acid glucoside, prepared by above                method; anda male anti-wrinkle eye cream, comprising                ascorbic acid glucoside, emulsifying agent,                emollient, thickening agent, emulsifying                stabilizer, humectant, chelating agent,                antioxidant, pH regulator and water.
