TI  - Preparing pentanediamine by using immobilized            lysine decarboxylase comprises e.g. constructing fusion            protein granules by e.g. extracting lysine            decarboxylase gene CadA and chitin binding domain gene            ChBD gene, and ligating gene fragment
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - Preparing pentanediamine by using immobilized                lysine decarboxylase comprises e.g. (i)                constructing fusion protein granules by extracting                lysine decarboxylase gene CadA and chitin binding                domain gene ChBD gene, ligating the gene fragment                to the ChBD gene in an empty plasmid pET-29a(+) by                using ligation and transformation of the CadA gene,                in which the ChBD gene is ligated to the N-terminus                of the CadA gene, transferring into a plasmid                pET-29a(+)-Chbd-Cada, then transferring into a                cloning vector Trans1-T1, screening on Lysogeny                broth plate, verifying colony by using colony PCR,                sequencing, culturing the correct sequencing                strain, and transforming is into an expression                vector BL21 (DE3) to obtain a genetically                engineered bacteria containing a lysine                decarboxylase fusion protein, and (ii) preparing                lysine decarboxylase crude enzyme solution by                culturing genetically engineered bacteria                containing lysine decarboxylase fusion protein, and                adding a seed solution to Lysogeny broth                medium.
                    USE - The method is useful for preparing                pentanediamine by using immobilized lysine                decarboxylase.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method: is suitable for repeatedly                producing 1,5-pentane pentamine; is economical; and                simplifies the separation step of the downstream                product and the enzyme.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - Preparing pentanediamine by using immobilized                lysine decarboxylase comprises (i) constructing                fusion protein granules by extracting lysine                decarboxylase gene CadA and chitin binding domain                gene ChBD gene, ligating the gene fragment to the                ChBD gene in an empty plasmid pET-29a(+) by using                ligation and transformation of the CadA gene, in                which the ChBD gene is ligated to the N-terminus of                the CadA gene, transferring into a plasmid                pET-29a(+)-Chbd-Cada, then transferring into a                cloning vector Trans1-T1, screening on the Lysogeny                broth plate, verifying the colony by using colony                PCR, sequencing, culturing the correct sequencing                strain, and transforming is into an expression                vector BL21 (DE3) to obtain a genetically                engineered bacteria containing a lysine                decarboxylase fusion protein, (ii) preparing lysine                decarboxylase crude enzyme solution by culturing                the genetically engineered bacteria containing the                lysine decarboxylase fusion protein, adding a seed                solution to the Lysogeny broth medium at a volume                fraction of 1-5 vol.% at 37&#176; C, when the                bacterial density OD600 is 0.4-0.6, collecting the                fermentation broth, inducing an induction agent for                12-14 hours, then centrifuging at 6000-8000 g in a                low temperature centrifuge to collect the strain,                washing for 2-5 times with distilled water, then                disrupting and centrifuging the cells at low                temperature, centrifuging at 6000-8000 g, and                collecting the supernatant to obtain a lysine                decarboxylase crude enzyme solution, (iii)                performing affinity adsorption of lysine                decarboxylase, adding 1-4 wt.% chitin to the lysine                decarboxylase crude enzyme solution, stirring at                4-37&#176; C for 100-400 revolutions/minute                (rpm), adjusting the pH to 5.6-8, and performing                affinity adsorption for 10-120 minutes to obtain an                immobilized enzyme, and (iv) preparing                1,5-pentanediamine by separating immobilized enzyme                from the crude enzyme solution, adding the                substrate lysine hydrochloride and the coenzyme                pyridoxal phosphate, stirring at 42&#176; C for                200-400 rpm, performing conversion reaction for 2-5                hours to obtain pentamethylenediamine conversion                solution, and recovering immobilized enzyme in the                conversion solution, where the substrate lysine                hydrochloride concentration is 100-200 g/l and the                coenzyme pyridoxal phosphate concentration is                0.05-0.2 mM.
