TI  - Recombinant Escherichia coli for producing            L-carnitine, comprises wild strain of Escherichia coli,            obtaining plasmids plasmids pEHcaiBCD and            pACYCD-caiT-caiF, and transforming into mutant strain            of Escherichia coli
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - Recombinant Escherichia coli comprises wild                strain BW25113 for encoding isocitrate                dehydrogenase phosphatase or kinase aceK, and gene                is deleted to obtain mutant strain of Escherichia                coli i.e. BW delta aceK. The anaerobic induction of                plasmid pETA is selected. The caiBCD fragment is                inserted in NdeI/KpnI cleavage site in multiple                cloning site to obtain first over-expression                plasmid pEH-caiBCD. The caiT inserted is into                pACYCD NdeI/XhoI site, caiF into pACYCD Hind                III/EcoR I sites to obtain second over-expression                plasmid pACYCD-caiT-caiF.
                    USE - Recombinant Escherichia coli for producing                L-carnitine (claimed).
                    ADVANTAGE - The recombinant bacteria Escherichia coli                enables to produce high yield L-carnitine from                crotonobetaine that has high substrate efficiency                in simple, economical and eco-friendly                manner.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - Recombinant Escherichia coli comprises wild                strain BW25113 for encoding isocitrate                dehydrogenase phosphatase or kinase aceK, and gene                is deleted to obtain mutant strain of Escherichia                coli i.e. BW delta aceK. The anaerobic induction of                plasmid pETA is selected. The caiBCD fragment is                inserted in NdeI/KpnI cleavage site in multiple                cloning site to obtain first over-expression                plasmid pEH-caiBCD. The caiT inserted is into                pACYCD NdeI/XhoI site, caiF into pACYCD Hind                III/EcoR I sites to obtain second over-expression                plasmid pACYCD-caiT-caiF. The two over-expression                plasmids pEHcaiBCD and pACYCD-caiT-caiF are                simultaneously transformed into Escherichia coli                mutant BW delta aceK to obtain produce L-carnitine.                INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for:(1) a method for producing recombinant                Escherichia coli, which involves taking wild strain                of Escherichia coli BW25113, and deleting aceK gene                to obtain mutant strain of Escherichia coli BW                delta aceK;(2) designing forward and reverse primers for                amplifying CaiBCD, caiF and caiT fragments, where                caiF forward primer and reverse primer comprises 34                and 33 nucleobases (SEQ ID NOs: 3and 4), and caiT                forward primer and reverse primer comprises 34                nucleobases (SEQ ID NOs: 5and 6), given in the                specification;(3) selecting anaerobically induced promoter                plasmid pET-A as the carrier, obtaining pEH-caiBCD                and pACYCD-caiT-caiF plasmids; and transforming in                Escherichia coli; and(4) a method for producing L-carnitine, which                involves amplifying recombinant bacteria for                preparing whole cell enzyme source, connecting                enzyme-producing culture medium BW delta                aceK/pEH-caiBCD ans pACYCD caiT-caiF, culturing                aerobically and then anaerobically, centrifugation                at 0-10 degrees C and 8000-12000 revolution per                minute, collecting cells, washing cells with                10-100mmol/l phosphate buffer, preparing conversion                reaction solution containing crotonobetaine                substrate, adding bacterial culture having cell                concentration 10-50g/l, and pouring reaction                mixture into shaker.
