AB  - This meeting, which focuses on neurology, neurosurgery and psychiatry, contains approximately 244 oral abstracts and 1 article in English. Topics include vascular disease and risk assessment in Parkinson's disease, efficacy and adverse effects of anti epileptic drugs, contemporary analysis of mortality in multiple sclerosis, eslicarbazepine acetate in previous carbamazepine non-responders, three years of changes in video-EEG telemetry surveillance, symptoms and acceptance of psychogenic non-epileptic seizures, and corticobasal syndrome and corticobasal degeneration. Other topics are comparing stimulus-presentation methods in temporal discrimintation testing, improving provision of Parkinson's disease exercise classes, rare structural genetic variation in human prion diseases, and treating multiple sclerosis with cladribine.
