TI  - Composition for treating CNS disease e.g.            neuropathy, amyloidosis, cancer, inflammation, and            Alzheimer's disease comprises molecule that binds            specific member of low density lipoprotein receptor            family and at least one CNS-active compound
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - A composition (C1) comprises: an LRP8 (member                of low density lipoprotein receptor family)-binding                molecule and at least one CNS-active                compound.
                    USE - For treating CNS disease or disorder selected                from neuropathy, amyloidosis, cancer, ocular                disease or disorder, viral or microbial infection,                inflammation, ischemia, neurodegenerative disease,                seizure, behavioral disorder, lysosomal storage                disease, Parkinson's disease, and Alzheimer's                disease; for diagnosing CNS disease or disorder;                and for staging CNS disease or CNS disorder                (claimed). The neuropathy disorders include chronic                pain (including nociceptive pain and cancer-related                pain), neuropathic pain, psychogenic pain,                headache, and migraine. The amyloidoses include                secondary amyloidosis, age-related amyloidosis,                Alzheimer's disease, mild cognitive impairment,                Lewy body dementia, Down's syndrome, hereditary                cerebral hemorrhage with amyloidosis (Dutch type),                Guam Parkinson-dementia complex, cerebral amyloid                angiopathy, Huntington's disease, progressive                supranuclear palsy, multiple sclerosis, Creutzfeld                Jacob disease, transmissible spongiform                encephalopathy, HIV-related dementia, amyotrophic                lateral sclerosis, and ocular diseases relating to                beta-amyloid deposition. The ocular diseases or                disorders include scleritis, keratitis, corneal                ulcer, corneal neovascularization, Fuchs'                dystrophy, keratoconus, keratoconjunctivitis sicca,                iritis, uveitis, retinal detachment, retinoschisis,                hypertensive retinopathy, diabetic retinopathy,                macular degeneration, epiretinal membrane,                retinitis pigmentosa, macular edema, glaucoma,                Leber's hereditary optic neuropathy, optic disc                drusen, myopia, astigmatism, anisometropia,                presbyopia, ophthalmoplegia, and xerophthalmia. The                viral or microbial infections of CNS include                infections by viruses (e.g. influenza, HIV,                poliovirus, and rubella), bacteria (e.g. Neisseria                species , Streptococcus species , Pseudomonas                species , Pneumococcus species , Meningococcus                species , Haemophilus species , and Mycobacterium                tuberculosis ), and other microorganisms such as                fungi (e.g. yeast, and Cryptococcus neoformans ),                parasites (e.g. Toxoplasma gondii ), and amoebas                resulting in CNS pathophysiologies such as                meningitis, encephalitis, myelitis, vasculitis and                abscess. Ischemia of CNS include focal brain                ischemia, global brain ischemia, stroke (i.e.                subarachnoid hemorrhage and intracerebral                hemorrhage), and aneurysm. The neurodegenerative                diseases include adrenoleukodystrophy, Alexander's                disease, ataxia telangiectasia, cockayne syndrome,                Friedreich's ataxia, Kennedy's disease, and                multiple system atrophy. The seizure diseases and                disorders of CNS include epilepsy, infantile                spasms, psychogenic seizures, and Lafora disease.                The behavioral disorders include insomnia,                parasomnias, night terrors, circadian rhythm sleep                disorders, narcolepsy, depression, anxiety,                phobias, panic attacks, obsessive-compulsive                disorder, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder,                chronic fatigue syndrome, agoraphobia,                post-traumatic stress disorder, bipolar disorder,                anorexia, bulimia, psychoses, autism, Rett's                syndrome, Asperger's syndrome, schizophrenia, and                delusional disorder. The lysosomal storage                disorders are metabolic disorders including                Tay-Sachs disease, Gaucher's disease, Fabry                disease, mucopolysaccharidosis, glycogen storage                disease, leukodystrophy, Farber's disease,                Canavan's leukodystrophy, neuronal ceroid                lipofuscinoses, Niemann-Pick disease, and Krabbe's                disease. The diagnosis of the CNS disease or                disorder involves detecting the disease or disorder                before onset of symptoms; assessment of severity or                duration of disease or disorder; or noninvasive                detection and/or imaging of disease or disorder,                where imaging is by radiography, tomography, or                magnetic resonance imaging.
                    ADVANTAGE - The composition provides therapeutic and                diagnostic composition capable of crossing blood                brain barrier and entering brain to exert                therapeutic and/or diagnostic functions. The                binding of LRP8-binding molecule to LRP8 effects                transport of CNS-active compound across blood-brain                barrier. The LRP8 specifically binds to LRP8 and                effects transmigration or translocation of compound                across blood brain barrier, so that CNS-active                compound has therapeutic and/or diagnostic function                desirable in brain. LRP8 is much more specifically                expressed in the brain/blood-brain barrier than                other described transporters. Thus the composition                offers alternative to the highly invasive and                generally unsatisfactory methods for bypassing                blood brain barrier, and allows agents e.g.                peptides, proteins and antibodies to cross blood                brain barrier from peripheral blood, by using                endogenous transport system mechanism to transport                desired substance from peripheral blood to CNS. The                composition (C1) modulates the transport of                CNS-active compound across blood-brain barrier in a                mammal by modulating the expression, stability, or                activity of LRP8; and modulates transport of                CNS-active compound across vascular endothelial                cell layer including tight junctions by targeting                LRP8. The composition also addresses key factor                important in delivering agent across blood brain                barrier to CNS that has not yet been solved i.e.                brain-specific delivery to brain. No highly                brain-specific receptor-mediated delivery has yet                been described. Most receptors previously utilized                for delivery are also highly expressed in                peripheral tissues, making solely brain-specific                delivery impossible with those molecules. The                advantages of improved brain-specificity are higher                efficacy of administered compound, as well as fewer                potential side effects at given dose of the                compound. The composition provides finding that                LRP8 is highly blood brain barrier-specific protein                that can be exploited to facilitate translocation                of other molecules normally unable to penetrate                into brain across blood brain barrier, including                biologic molecules such as antibodies.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a                pharmaceutical formulation (C2) comprising: the                composition (C1) and a carrier.
