TI  - Rydberg-atom electromagnetic field detector            apparatus for detecting electromagnetic field in radio            receiver of e.g. radiodetermination system, in wireless            telecommunications network, has waveguide for guiding            propagation of first and second EM fields towards first            and second RAEM-FDs
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The apparatus (100) has a first Rydberg-atom                electromagnetic field detector (RAEM-FD) (107-1)                for detecting first EM field (170-1). A second                RAEM-FD (107-2) detects second EM field (170-2). A                waveguide (105) guides propagation of the first and                second EM field towards the first and second                RAEM-FDs, where the first EM field is different                from the second EM field in frequency, modulation                and transmit power. The waveguide comprises a                multi-plate waveguide (MPWG), a tapered-plate                waveguide (TPWG), a parallel-plate waveguide                (PPWG), a horn and a lens. The second RAEM-FD is                arranged downstream of the first RAEM-FD and the                waveguide.
                    USE - RAEM-FD apparatus for detecting an EM field in                a radio receiver (claimed) of a radiodetermination                system, a medical imaging device, an MRI and                magnetic resonance spectroscopy system, a                radio-imaging system and a composition analysis                instrument for a wireless telecommunications                network.
                    ADVANTAGE - The single probe laser and the single coupling                laser are shared by the RAEM-FDs so as to reduce                cost and complexity of the apparatus. The EM field                detector comprises the RAEM-FDs, with appropriate                coupling to the waveguide so as to increase                bandwidth, redundancy and resilience and                simultaneously focus more EM fields of different                frequencies upon the RAEM-FDs. The the RAEM-FDs are                encased within the waveguide, which provides a                closed metal enclosure so as to permit an E-field                of the EM fields to oscillate inside the enclosure,                thus enhancing signal intensity at vapor                cells.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic view of an EM                field detector comprising a waveguide.100RAEM-FD apparatus105Waveguide107-1RAEM-FD107-2Second RAEM-FD170-1First EM field170-2Second EM field
