TI  - Building Healthcare Applications with LiDAR - Real-time Tissue Identification for Surgery
T2  - 2024 IEEE HEALTHCARE INNOVATIONS AND POINT OF CARE TECHNOLOGIES, HI-POCT
M3  - Proceedings Paper
CP  - 2024 Conference on Healthcare Innovations and Point of Care Technologies
CL  - Tucson, AZ
AB  - In this work, we explored the use of an industrial precision handheld Laser Line Probe (LLP) with 25-micron accuracy to extract tissue viscoelastic information, with the goal of identifying healthy and cancerous tissue in real-time. This would contribute to significantly improved surgical outcomes, with scalability to resource limited environments.Reliable simulation of intraoperative palpation was achieved by keeping the LLP constant and during direct probing of a liver high fidelity tissue model. This produced a point cloud which emulated time-series data with the scan line progressively forming a depression. By extracting physical and 3D point cloud features, we trained a Random Forest model capable of classifying biophantom and non-organic samples with a 96% 10-fold cross-validation accuracy.
