TI  - Study on Insulation Characteristic of PET Based on HN Dielectric Relaxation Model
T2  - 2022 4TH ASIA ENERGY AND ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING SYMPOSIUM (AEEES 2022)
M3  - Proceedings Paper
CP  - 4th Asia Energy and Electrical Engineering Symposium (AEEES)
CL  - Chengdu, PEOPLES R CHINA
AB  - SF6 gas-insulated transformers are widely used as an environmentally friendly transformer, where PET films are used as winding insulation. In this paper, we investigated the frequency domain dielectric spectrum of aged PET films at different measurement temperatures. And the experimental data were fitted with the Havriliak-Negami dielectric relaxation model(HN dielectric relaxation model). It is found that the relaxation time constant shows a linear logarithmic relationship with the measurement temperature and satisfies the Arrhenius equation; With the decrease of aging temperature and the increase of measuring temperature, the relaxation time decreases and the frequency of peak increases.
