TI  - Aging evaluation method for polyethylene            terephthalate material of gas insulating transformer,            involves determining equivalent aging time of            polyethylene terephthalate material based on aging            state evaluation parameter through preset equivalent            aging time algorithm
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves measuring polyethylene                terephthalate material of a gas insulating                transformer to be evaluated by a Frequency Domain                Spectroscopy (FDS) dielectric spectrum tester to                obtain corresponding frequency domain dielectric                spectrum function. The frequency domain dielectric                spectrum function is calculated by preset                relaxation peak analysis algorithm. Number of                relaxation process contained in the frequency                domain dielectric spectrum function is determined.                A H-N relaxation model to be applied is determined                based on the number of relaxation process. The H-N                relaxation model to be applied is used for fitting                the frequency domain dielectric spectrum curve to                obtain aging state evaluation parameter                corresponding to the frequency domain dielectric                spectrum function. Equivalent aging time of the                polyethylene terephthalate material is determined                based on the aging state evaluation parameter                through the preset equivalent aging time                algorithm.
                    USE - Aging evaluation method for polyethylene                terephthalate material of a gas insulating                transformer used in underground substation in large                and middle cities and densely populated areas such                as business centers and hospitals.
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables evaluating the aging state                of the winding insulating PET material in the gas                insulating transformer accurately and                effectively.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - The aging state of the polyethylene                terephthalate material is determined based on the                equivalent aging time.INDEPENDENT CLAIMS are included for:(1) an aging evaluation device for PET                material of a gas insulating transformer;(2) a non-volatile computer storage medium                stored with computer executable instruction for                aging evaluation of a gas insulating transformer                PET material.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a flow diagram illustrating                an Aging evaluation method for polyethylene                terephthalate material of a gas insulating                transformer. (Drawing includes non-English language                text).
