TI  - System for processing mixed waste, has separation            tank which is adapted to separate organic fraction in            slurry into more refined organic fraction and residual            non-organic fraction using organic/non-organic            fractions relative densities
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The system (10) has a wet separation station                (200) that is set with a separation tank for                receiving slurry comprising a mixture of the                organic fraction from the separator and water. The                separation tank is adapted to separate the organic                fraction in the slurry into a more refined organic                fraction and a residual non-organic fraction using                relative densities of the more refined organic                fraction and the residual non-organic fraction. A                dewatering station (300) is configured to receive                and dewater slurry from the wet separation station                containing the more refined organic fraction.
                    USE - System for processing mixed waste such as                municipal solid waste (MSW) (claimed), commercial                and industrial waste, street sweepings, food waste                and food and green waste. Uses include but are not                limited to discarded material such as discarded                apparel, packaging and paper of various forms,                plant matter, nappies, household pet waste and                recyclable material such as plastics, glass and                metal containers, paper and cardboard.
                    ADVANTAGE - The reuse of significant proportion of MSW is                facilitated that is likely to be sent to landfill.                The processing feedstock obtained from MSW is                facilitated to reclaim both organic fraction having                a quality suitable for use as compost and high                calorific materials for use as an input for                producing a process engineered fuel.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is included for a method                for processing mixed waste.
