TI  - Method for displaying selected programming            material on e.g. personal computer, involves receiving            programming material from remote server, and displaying            selected programming material on display
AB  - 
                   NOVELTY - The method involves recognizing a machine                recognizable feature of a printed matter (40) using                a feature recognizing device. Encoded data                associated with the machine recognizable feature of                the printed matter is identified. The encoded data                associated with the machine recognizable feature is                transmitted to a remote server (30) using a user                device. Programming material selected from a set of                programming materials associated with the machine                recognizable feature based on user preference is                received from the remote server. The selected                programming material is displayed on a                display.
                    USE - Method for displaying selected programming                material on a user device e.g. personal computer,                hand-held communication device, cellular telephone,                camera-enabled cellular telephone, scanner,                personal digital assistant, internet-enabled                telephone, Internet-enabled device and TV, by                machine recognizable feature e.g. code, barcode,                two-dimensional barcode, biometric sample,                watermark, digital watermark, transponder, radio                frequency identification device tag and touch                sensor, within printed matter e.g. book, textbook,                newspaper, editorial, advertisement, magazine,                passport, boarding pass, real estate listing,                identification card, smart card, license, receipt,                business card, credit card and cash card, and user                profile with user preference e.g. medical                information such as medical history, record of                allergic reactions, prescription medication                history, hospitalization history, surgical                operation history, medical illness history, family                medical illness history, medical imaging test                result, laboratory test result, test result                selected from MRI scan, computed tomography (CT)                scan, position emission tomography (PET) scan,                X-ray, electroencephalograph (EEG), blood test and                urine analysis test, musical preference e.g.                artist, genre, time period and playlist, food                preference e.g. seasonal information, location of                origin, classification, organic or non-organic,                ethnicity of food and nutritional information,                recreational preference such as sport of interest,                favorite sports team, favorite sport venue, type of                art, artist, recreational activity, recreational                establishment and recreational venue, occupation                information e.g. occupational title, occupational                preference, job preference, benefits preference,                occupational industry, location of occupation,                occupational history, occupational trajectory,                current or desired salary and current or desired                occupational work hour, real estate preference such                as property location, property listing, property                value, property size, property listing price,                property layout and comparative property, travel                preference e.g. travel history, number of                travelers, age of the travelers, desired location,                type of lodging, climate, activity, food or meal                plan and occupational travel, product preference                e.g. brand, cost, quality, features, duration of                use, quantity and location of use, dating                preference such as demographic information,                prospective dating partner's demographic                information and user's or prospective dating                partner's age, gender, ethnicity, occupation,                educational level, religion, family background,                interest, hobby, political orientation, income                level, physical characteristic, weight, height,                race, hair color and eye color, educational history                e.g. college or university attended, degree earned,                major area of study, year of degree conferral,                educational trajectory and subject studied,                shopping preference e.g. store, vendor, location of                the store or vendor, distance from the store or                vendor, age, clothing size and clothing style,                clothing color preference, store classification and                religious preference such as religious history,                religious denomination, current religious belief,                desired religious service, location of religious                practice and desired religious information, and                political preference e.g. political history,                political ideology, current political party                affiliation, preferred political candidate,                political activity and learning style (all                claimed).
                    ADVANTAGE - The method enables a user to select and                control the presentation of audio/video programming                through a familiar printed matter interface, thus                offering universal accessibility. The method                enables a set of URLs reflecting a set of web sites                and web pages to be encoded in the machine                recognizable feature for providing the user with                opportunity to select the web sites and the web                pages containing user preferred information to                access before transmitting a command to a                processing unit associated with the remote server,                thus delivering most appropriate content, and hence                providing an improved user-interface for retrieval                of electronic data by using the user profile stored                on the remote server at low cost.
                    DETAILED DESCRIPTION - An INDEPENDENT CLAIM is also included for a                system for displaying selected programming material                to a user.
                    DESCRIPTION Of DRAWING(S) - The drawing shows a schematic block diagram                of a system for displaying selected programming                material in which a display unit is embedded within                a feature recognition unit.30Remote server40Printed matter46Recognition/control unit47Display unit80Display
